Upstream commit dbbd04de7ec48f8aa9311d32ecd557ce44c630af (mautrix/gmessages main, 2026-10-17, not in v0.2610.0):
"chatsync: run DM dedup row delete inside its transaction (#103)", by Gerardo Rodriguez, applied to 186284e,
with a regression test of ours (pkg/connector/chatsync_dedup_test.go).

Why: deduplicateDM's delete ran on the outer context, so on SQLite with _txlock=immediate it waited on another
connection for the write lock its own transaction held, failed after the 5 s busy timeout, rolled the change back,
and the error was swallowed, so the same change was tried again on every conversation event. On the cloud host
(2026-10-20 logs) that held the bridge's write lock about 5 s out of every 5: every other write waited too, and a
10-line reply reached Google one line per stall. The test takes 5.3 s and fails without the fix, 0.2 s with it.

